    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying your name",
     "texto": [
      "There are two ways to say what your name is, and both are correct:\n\n- **Me llamo Ana.**\n- **Soy Ana.**\n\nTo ask: **¿Cómo te llamas?**\n\nSpanish almost never needs the pronoun. «Soy» already says «I am», so «yo soy» is only used when you want to insist."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The verb ser",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **ser** is used for a name, origin and nationality.\n\n- yo **soy**\n- tú **eres**\n- él / ella / usted **es**\n\nNotice that each form already says who is speaking, which is why the pronoun is almost never needed."
     ],
